[agent:result] Execute one or more SQL statements against a Databricks SQL warehouse
[agent:result] and return results.
[agent:result] 
[agent:result] A single SQL can be provided as a positional argument, read from a file with
[agent:result] --file, or piped via stdin. If a positional argument ends in .sql and the
[agent:result] file exists, it is read as a SQL file automatically.
[agent:result] 
[agent:result] Pass multiple positional arguments and/or repeat --file to run several
[agent:result] queries in parallel against the warehouse. Multi-query output is always
[agent:result] JSON: an array of {sql, statement_id, state, elapsed_ms, columns, rows,
[agent:result] error} objects. Result order is: --file inputs first (in flag order),
[agent:result] then positional SQLs (in arg order). The exit code is non-zero if any
[agent:result] query failed.
[agent:result] 
[agent:result] The command auto-detects an available warehouse unless --warehouse is set
[agent:result] or the DATABRICKS_WAREHOUSE_ID environment variable is configured.
[agent:result] 
[agent:result] For a single query, output is JSON in non-interactive contexts. In
[agent:result] interactive terminals it renders tables, and large results open an
[agent:result] interactive table browser. Use --output csv to export results as CSV.
[agent:result] 
[agent:result] Pass named parameters with --param. Use ":name" markers in the SQL and
[agent:result] "--param name=value" (string) or "--param name:TYPE=value" (typed, e.g.
[agent:result] DATE, INT) to bind values. Positional "?" markers are not supported. In
[agent:result] multi-query mode, the same parameter set is applied to every statement.
[agent:result] 
